course: dictionary
lesson: 3541
title: Feeble: weak and not good enough
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Feeble means very weak, with little strength or energy. Look at the words around it for clues. «At last a feeble voice answers from an old beech tree.» A voice that comes out faintly and slowly is weak, not loud, so feeble must mean weak.
explain: Feeble can also mean not good enough or not convincing. «That's a feeble excuse!» tells you the reason does not work. Test it by swapping in weak: «That's a weak excuse!» still makes sense, so you know you have the right meaning.
explain: Feeble is used for things too. «Feeble light» is dim light, a light that does not shine strongly. «The Rat tried a feeble jig in the snow» shows a dance with no energy in it. Ask yourself: is this strong, or is it weak?
fact: Feeble means very weak, without strength or energy.
fact: Feeble also means not good enough or not convincing, as in «a feeble excuse» or «a feeble joke».
fact: «Feeble light» means dim light.
fact: The Rat cried «Hooray!» and then «fell to executing a feeble jig in the snow»; a jig is a lively hopping dance.
fact: Feeble has comparison forms: feeble, feebler, feeblest.
exercise: «At last a feeble voice answers from an old beech tree.» What does feeble mean here? | Angry and rude | Hidden under the tree | *Very weak, with little strength | Very loud and cheerful
exercise: Jayden says «That's a feeble excuse!» What does Jayden mean? | It is a kind thing to say | It is a clever reason, well done | It is a very long excuse | *It is not a good reason
exercise: Bill is «feeble and squeaky» when he speaks. What does feeble suggest about Bill's voice? | Strong and deep | Fast and clear | *Weak and quiet | Happy and loud
test: Which word means about the same as feeble in «feeble light»? | Warm | Coloured | *Dim | Bright
test: «fell to executing a feeble jig in the snow». What is a jig? | A loud shout | A sleepy nap | A cold walk in the snow | *A lively hopping dance
exam: The Rat cried «Hooray!» and then did a «feeble jig in the snow». What does feeble tell you about the jig? | It was a dance for a big party | It was a famous sport | It was fast, loud and perfect | *It was weak, with little energy in it
